sequenceDiagram
  %% Container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/development-containers.md#t3-registration-and-pairing, docs/reference/conn.md#renewal-of-an-instance-server): how Orbit keeps the Gateway's admin session on a container's T3 server. The create flow registers the server (built, steps clone-sessions and clone-register of workflow-operation-instance-create). This chart is its renewal, `conn.environment_renew`, workflow-operation-conn-environment-renew. The container cannot call the Gateway, so the Gateway records the session from the run's result.
  %% status: built
  %% command: none · hourly tick, and POST /conn/environments/{environment_id}/renew
  %% kind: conn.environment_renew
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Conn layer
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Node<br/>the container
  Note over GW: Find sessions to renew<br/>hourly · under 7 days left
  %%> When:
  %%> - each session of an active Instance's T3 server that ends within seven days, or has ended
  %%> - the route admits one at once, also past the wait below
  %%> - a successful `instance.wake` admits one at once for its Instance (instance/wake.mmd), outside the limits below; the wake also renews the Instance's held sessions that end within seven days
  %%> Skips:
  %%> - a sleeping Instance (`power_state` `stopped`): its wake renews it
  %%> Limits:
  %%> - at most five a tick, the earliest end first; one a Node at a time
  %%> - after `conn.environment_stopped`, the server waits six hours
  %%> Result:
  %%> - one Operation a server, holding the server's lock; the intent has no session
  %%> Same tick, afterwards:
  %%> - the held sessions of Nodes (session-hold.mmd): withdraw a session whose Node lost its grant, renew each that ends within seven days, those whose last renewal failed last, admit each owed revoke while its server runs
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-conn-environment-renew
  SW->>N: Issue the Gateway session<br/>t3 auth session issue
  %%> Command, over the Node's SSH account, then in the container as `agent`:
  %%> - `t3 auth session issue --label "Orbit Gateway" --json`, into a 0600 file of the SSH account
  %%> Refuses first:
  %%> - a stopped container, `conn.environment_stopped`; no container, `conn.environment_missing`
  %%> Why no old session:
  %%> - an ended session renews too, so a container stopped past its end comes back
  SW->>N: Copy the session<br/>to the worker
  SW->>SW: Store the session<br/>one authenticated read
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the copy, then reads `/.well-known/t3/environment` and `/api/auth/session` at the recorded URL, the path a pairing takes
  %%> - the id must be the recorded one, else `conn.environment_mismatch`; T3 must accept the session with `access:read` and `access:write`
  %%> - only then stores it as a native sensitive field
  SW->>N: Remove the copies<br/>on every path
  alt the session is proven
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>vault key · end
    Note over GW: Record the session
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stores the session encrypted, clears the last refusal, deletes the vault copy
    %%> Result:
    %%> - then admits the cleanup that revokes older `Orbit Gateway` sessions; it waits while a pairing or a held-session run that carries the old session runs
    %%> - then renews the server's held sessions that end within seven days, which waited for this session
  else a step refused
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>conn.* code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the old session stays; the server record keeps the code and its time, and the next tick tries again
  end
